IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `cpp-core`
IMPORT `cpp-core-calendar`
IMPORT `cpp-core-age`
IMPORT `cp3-nouns`
IMPORT `cp3-deemed-contributions`

-- Tests of cp3-deemed-contributions.l4 (sections 52, 52.1 and 52.2). Expected values are written by
-- hand from the text. A person born on 10 March 1990 reaches 18 on 10 March 2008; section 2(2) deems
-- the age reached on 1 April 2008, so the months of 2008 "after they reached that age" are April to
-- December: nine months.

GIVEN dob IS A DATE
      died IS A MAYBE DATE
      started IS A MAYBE DATE
      ceased IS A MAYBE DATE
      excluded IS A LIST OF DATE
GIVETH A `cp3 Life events of a contributor`
`the deemed-contributions test events` dob died started ceased excluded MEANS
    `cp3 Life events of a contributor` WITH
        `the contributor's date of birth` IS dob
        `the day the contributor died, if the contributor has died` IS died
        `the month with which a retirement pension becomes payable, if it does` IS started
        `the month in which a disability pension ceased to be payable, if it did` IS ceased
        `the months excluded from the contributory period by reason of disability` IS excluded

§ `Tests -- section 52`

§§ `52(1) -- the months of a year`

-- no event in the year: all twelve months, and 12000 / 12 = 1000 a month
#ASSERT count (`s 52(1) — the months of a year for which the base contribution is deemed to have been made` 2009 (`the deemed-contributions test events` (YearMonthDay 1990 3 10) NOTHING NOTHING NOTHING EMPTY)) EQUALS 12
#ASSERT `s 52(1) — the earnings for which the base contribution is deemed to have been made for each month of a year` 2009 (`the deemed-contributions test events` (YearMonthDay 1990 3 10) NOTHING NOTHING NOTHING EMPTY) 12000 EQUALS JUST 1000
-- the year of the 18th birthday: April to December, nine months; 9000 / 9 = 1000
#ASSERT count (`s 52(1) — the months of a year for which the base contribution is deemed to have been made` 2008 (`the deemed-contributions test events` (YearMonthDay 1990 3 10) NOTHING NOTHING NOTHING EMPTY)) EQUALS 9
#ASSERT `s 52(1) — the earnings for which the base contribution is deemed to have been made for each month of a year` 2008 (`the deemed-contributions test events` (YearMonthDay 1990 3 10) NOTHING NOTHING NOTHING EMPTY) 9000 EQUALS JUST 1000
-- March 2008 is before the age is deemed reached; April 2008 is the first month after
#ASSERT NOT `s 52(1) — a month is one for which the base contribution is deemed to have been made` (YearMonthDay 2008 3 1) (`the deemed-contributions test events` (YearMonthDay 1990 3 10) NOTHING NOTHING NOTHING EMPTY)
#ASSERT `s 52(1) — a month is one for which the base contribution is deemed to have been made` (YearMonthDay 2008 4 1) (`the deemed-contributions test events` (YearMonthDay 1990 3 10) NOTHING NOTHING NOTHING EMPTY)
-- a birthday in December: the age is deemed reached on 1 January of the next year, so that is the year of paragraph (a)
-- born 15 December 1990: reaches 18 on 15 December 2008, deemed 1 January 2009: all of 2009 follows
#ASSERT count (`s 52(1) — the months of a year for which the base contribution is deemed to have been made` 2009 (`the deemed-contributions test events` (YearMonthDay 1990 12 15) NOTHING NOTHING NOTHING EMPTY)) EQUALS 12
#ASSERT count (`s 52(1) — the months of a year for which the base contribution is deemed to have been made` 2008 (`the deemed-contributions test events` (YearMonthDay 1990 12 15) NOTHING NOTHING NOTHING EMPTY)) EQUALS 12
-- the year of the 70th birthday: born 20 June 1950, 70 on 20 June 2020, deemed 1 July 2020: January to June, six months; 6000 / 6 = 1000
#ASSERT count (`s 52(1) — the months of a year for which the base contribution is deemed to have been made` 2020 (`the deemed-contributions test events` (YearMonthDay 1950 6 20) NOTHING NOTHING NOTHING EMPTY)) EQUALS 6
#ASSERT `s 52(1) — the earnings for which the base contribution is deemed to have been made for each month of a year` 2020 (`the deemed-contributions test events` (YearMonthDay 1950 6 20) NOTHING NOTHING NOTHING EMPTY) 6000 EQUALS JUST 1000
#ASSERT `s 52(1) — a month is one for which the base contribution is deemed to have been made` (YearMonthDay 2020 6 1) (`the deemed-contributions test events` (YearMonthDay 1950 6 20) NOTHING NOTHING NOTHING EMPTY)
#ASSERT NOT `s 52(1) — a month is one for which the base contribution is deemed to have been made` (YearMonthDay 2020 7 1) (`the deemed-contributions test events` (YearMonthDay 1950 6 20) NOTHING NOTHING NOTHING EMPTY)
-- born 15 December 1950: 70 on 15 December 2020, deemed 1 January 2021: 2020 is whole, 2021 has no month left (not covered)
#ASSERT count (`s 52(1) — the months of a year for which the base contribution is deemed to have been made` 2020 (`the deemed-contributions test events` (YearMonthDay 1950 12 15) NOTHING NOTHING NOTHING EMPTY)) EQUALS 12
#ASSERT `s 52(1) — the earnings for which the base contribution is deemed to have been made for each month of a year` 2021 (`the deemed-contributions test events` (YearMonthDay 1950 12 15) NOTHING NOTHING NOTHING EMPTY) 4000 EQUALS NOTHING
-- death on 14 September 2015: the months before it, January to August
#ASSERT count (`s 52(1) — the months of a year for which the base contribution is deemed to have been made` 2015 (`the deemed-contributions test events` (YearMonthDay 1960 1 1) (JUST (YearMonthDay 2015 9 14)) NOTHING NOTHING EMPTY)) EQUALS 8
#ASSERT NOT `s 52(1) — a month is one for which the base contribution is deemed to have been made` (YearMonthDay 2015 9 1) (`the deemed-contributions test events` (YearMonthDay 1960 1 1) (JUST (YearMonthDay 2015 9 14)) NOTHING NOTHING EMPTY)
-- a retirement pension payable with May 2018: the months before May, four
#ASSERT count (`s 52(1) — the months of a year for which the base contribution is deemed to have been made` 2018 (`the deemed-contributions test events` (YearMonthDay 1953 1 1) NOTHING (JUST (YearMonthDay 2018 5 1)) NOTHING EMPTY)) EQUALS 4
#ASSERT `s 52(1) — the earnings for which the base contribution is deemed to have been made for each month of a year` 2018 (`the deemed-contributions test events` (YearMonthDay 1953 1 1) NOTHING (JUST (YearMonthDay 2018 5 1)) NOTHING EMPTY) 2000 EQUALS JUST 500
-- a disability pension that ceased in August 2012: the months after August, four
#ASSERT count (`s 52(1) — the months of a year for which the base contribution is deemed to have been made` 2012 (`the deemed-contributions test events` (YearMonthDay 1970 1 1) NOTHING NOTHING (JUST (YearMonthDay 2012 8 1)) EMPTY)) EQUALS 4
#ASSERT NOT `s 52(1) — a month is one for which the base contribution is deemed to have been made` (YearMonthDay 2012 8 1) (`the deemed-contributions test events` (YearMonthDay 1970 1 1) NOTHING NOTHING (JUST (YearMonthDay 2012 8 1)) EMPTY)
-- January to March 2012 excluded by reason of disability: nine months left; 9000 / 9 = 1000
#ASSERT count (`s 52(1) — the months of a year for which the base contribution is deemed to have been made` 2012 (`the deemed-contributions test events` (YearMonthDay 1970 1 1) NOTHING NOTHING NOTHING (LIST (YearMonthDay 2012 1 1), (YearMonthDay 2012 2 1), (YearMonthDay 2012 3 1)))) EQUALS 9
#ASSERT `s 52(1) — the earnings for which the base contribution is deemed to have been made for each month of a year` 2012 (`the deemed-contributions test events` (YearMonthDay 1970 1 1) NOTHING NOTHING NOTHING (LIST (YearMonthDay 2012 1 1), (YearMonthDay 2012 2 1), (YearMonthDay 2012 3 1))) 9000 EQUALS JUST 1000
-- a month listed on a day other than its first is still that month
#ASSERT NOT `s 52(1) — a month is one for which the base contribution is deemed to have been made` (YearMonthDay 2012 2 1) (`the deemed-contributions test events` (YearMonthDay 1970 1 1) NOTHING NOTHING NOTHING (LIST (YearMonthDay 2012 2 17)))
-- two events in one year (excluded January to March and a pension stopping in August): a month must satisfy both limbs: September to December, four
#ASSERT count (`s 52(1) — the months of a year for which the base contribution is deemed to have been made` 2012 (`the deemed-contributions test events` (YearMonthDay 1970 1 1) NOTHING NOTHING (JUST (YearMonthDay 2012 8 1)) (LIST (YearMonthDay 2012 1 1), (YearMonthDay 2012 2 1), (YearMonthDay 2012 3 1)))) EQUALS 4

§§ `52(2) and 52(3)`

#ASSERT `s 52(2) — the earnings for which a base contribution is deemed to have been made for a month of a year with no base contribution` EQUALS 0
-- the earnings exceed the basic exemption: deemed made
#ASSERT `s 52(3)(a) — a base contribution is deemed to have been made for a year` 5000 3500
-- equal to the basic exemption: deemed not made ("exceed")
#ASSERT NOT `s 52(3)(a) — a base contribution is deemed to have been made for a year` 3500 3500
#ASSERT NOT `s 52(3)(a) — a base contribution is deemed to have been made for a year` 3499.99 3500
#ASSERT `s 52(3)(a) — a base contribution is deemed to have been made for a year` 3500.01 3500
#ASSERT `s 52(3)(b) — a base contribution is deemed to have been made for earnings for a month` (YearMonthDay 2009 5 1) (`the deemed-contributions test events` (YearMonthDay 1990 3 10) NOTHING NOTHING NOTHING EMPTY)
#ASSERT NOT `s 52(3)(b) — a base contribution is deemed to have been made for earnings for a month` (YearMonthDay 2008 2 1) (`the deemed-contributions test events` (YearMonthDay 1990 3 10) NOTHING NOTHING NOTHING EMPTY)

§§ `52 -- the earnings for one month`

-- a contribution made for the year: 12000 / 12 = 1000 for a month of the year
#ASSERT `s 52 — the earnings for which a base contribution is deemed to have been made for a month` (YearMonthDay 2009 5 1) (`the deemed-contributions test events` (YearMonthDay 1990 3 10) NOTHING NOTHING NOTHING EMPTY) 12000 3500 EQUALS 1000
-- a year of earnings that do not exceed the basic exemption: no contribution deemed, zero (subsection (2))
#ASSERT `s 52 — the earnings for which a base contribution is deemed to have been made for a month` (YearMonthDay 2009 5 1) (`the deemed-contributions test events` (YearMonthDay 1990 3 10) NOTHING NOTHING NOTHING EMPTY) 3500 3500 EQUALS 0
-- a month the subsection does not reach (January 2008, before the 18th birthday deemed): no earnings deemed for it
#ASSERT `s 52 — the earnings for which a base contribution is deemed to have been made for a month` (YearMonthDay 2008 1 1) (`the deemed-contributions test events` (YearMonthDay 1990 3 10) NOTHING NOTHING NOTHING EMPTY) 9000 3500 EQUALS 0
-- a month the subsection reaches in the year of the 18th birthday: 9000 / 9
#ASSERT `s 52 — the earnings for which a base contribution is deemed to have been made for a month` (YearMonthDay 2008 6 1) (`the deemed-contributions test events` (YearMonthDay 1990 3 10) NOTHING NOTHING NOTHING EMPTY) 9000 3500 EQUALS 1000

§ `Tests -- section 52.1`

-- 12 months with no event: 24000 / 12 = 2000
#ASSERT count (`s 52.1(1) — the months of a year for which the first additional contribution is deemed to have been made` 2021 (`the deemed-contributions test events` (YearMonthDay 1990 3 10) NOTHING NOTHING NOTHING EMPTY)) EQUALS 12
#ASSERT `s 52.1(1) — the earnings for which the first additional contribution is deemed to have been made for each month of a year` 2021 (`the deemed-contributions test events` (YearMonthDay 1990 3 10) NOTHING NOTHING NOTHING EMPTY) 24000 EQUALS JUST 2000
-- months excluded by reason of disability are not a limb of section 52.1: still twelve
#ASSERT count (`s 52.1(1) — the months of a year for which the first additional contribution is deemed to have been made` 2021 (`the deemed-contributions test events` (YearMonthDay 1990 3 10) NOTHING NOTHING (JUST (YearMonthDay 2021 8 1)) (LIST (YearMonthDay 2021 1 1), (YearMonthDay 2021 2 1)))) EQUALS 12
-- the year of the 18th birthday: nine months
#ASSERT count (`s 52.1(1) — the months of a year for which the first additional contribution is deemed to have been made` 2008 (`the deemed-contributions test events` (YearMonthDay 1990 3 10) NOTHING NOTHING NOTHING EMPTY)) EQUALS 9
-- the year of the 70th birthday, deemed 1 July 2020: six months
#ASSERT count (`s 52.1(1) — the months of a year for which the first additional contribution is deemed to have been made` 2020 (`the deemed-contributions test events` (YearMonthDay 1950 6 20) NOTHING NOTHING NOTHING EMPTY)) EQUALS 6
-- death in September and retirement pension from May in one year: months before May (the stricter limb): four
#ASSERT count (`s 52.1(1) — the months of a year for which the first additional contribution is deemed to have been made` 2018 (`the deemed-contributions test events` (YearMonthDay 1953 1 1) (JUST (YearMonthDay 2018 9 14)) (JUST (YearMonthDay 2018 5 1)) NOTHING EMPTY)) EQUALS 4
-- no month left: not covered
#ASSERT `s 52.1(1) — the earnings for which the first additional contribution is deemed to have been made for each month of a year` 2021 (`the deemed-contributions test events` (YearMonthDay 1950 12 15) NOTHING NOTHING NOTHING EMPTY) 1000 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 52.1(2) — the earnings for which a first additional contribution is deemed to have been made for a month of a year with no first additional contribution` EQUALS 0
-- exceeds the basic exemption: deemed made; equal: not
#ASSERT `s 52.1(3)(a) — a first additional contribution is deemed to have been made for a year` 3600 3500
#ASSERT NOT `s 52.1(3)(a) — a first additional contribution is deemed to have been made for a year` 3500 3500
#ASSERT `s 52.1(3)(b) — a first additional contribution is deemed to have been made for earnings for a month` (YearMonthDay 2021 5 1) (`the deemed-contributions test events` (YearMonthDay 1990 3 10) NOTHING NOTHING NOTHING EMPTY)
#ASSERT NOT `s 52.1(3)(b) — a first additional contribution is deemed to have been made for earnings for a month` (YearMonthDay 2008 2 1) (`the deemed-contributions test events` (YearMonthDay 1990 3 10) NOTHING NOTHING NOTHING EMPTY)
-- one month of a year: 24000 / 12
#ASSERT `s 52.1 — the earnings for which a first additional contribution is deemed to have been made for a month` (YearMonthDay 2021 5 1) (`the deemed-contributions test events` (YearMonthDay 1990 3 10) NOTHING NOTHING NOTHING EMPTY) 24000 3500 EQUALS 2000
-- first additional earnings that do not exceed the basic exemption: zero
#ASSERT `s 52.1 — the earnings for which a first additional contribution is deemed to have been made for a month` (YearMonthDay 2021 5 1) (`the deemed-contributions test events` (YearMonthDay 1990 3 10) NOTHING NOTHING NOTHING EMPTY) 3500 3500 EQUALS 0
-- a month the subsection does not reach: zero
#ASSERT `s 52.1 — the earnings for which a first additional contribution is deemed to have been made for a month` (YearMonthDay 2008 2 1) (`the deemed-contributions test events` (YearMonthDay 1990 3 10) NOTHING NOTHING NOTHING EMPTY) 9000 3500 EQUALS 0

§ `Tests -- section 52.2`

#ASSERT count (`s 52.2(1) — the months of a year for which the second additional contribution is deemed to have been made` 2025 (`the deemed-contributions test events` (YearMonthDay 1990 3 10) NOTHING NOTHING NOTHING EMPTY)) EQUALS 12
#ASSERT `s 52.2(1) — the earnings for which the second additional contribution is deemed to have been made for each month of a year` 2025 (`the deemed-contributions test events` (YearMonthDay 1990 3 10) NOTHING NOTHING NOTHING EMPTY) 6000 EQUALS JUST 500
-- death on 14 September 2025: eight months; 4000 / 8 = 500
#ASSERT count (`s 52.2(1) — the months of a year for which the second additional contribution is deemed to have been made` 2025 (`the deemed-contributions test events` (YearMonthDay 1960 1 1) (JUST (YearMonthDay 2025 9 14)) NOTHING NOTHING EMPTY)) EQUALS 8
#ASSERT `s 52.2(1) — the earnings for which the second additional contribution is deemed to have been made for each month of a year` 2025 (`the deemed-contributions test events` (YearMonthDay 1960 1 1) (JUST (YearMonthDay 2025 9 14)) NOTHING NOTHING EMPTY) 4000 EQUALS JUST 500
-- born 15 December 1950: 70 on 15 December 2020, deemed 1 January 2021: no month of 2021 is left
#ASSERT `s 52.2(1) — the earnings for which the second additional contribution is deemed to have been made for each month of a year` 2021 (`the deemed-contributions test events` (YearMonthDay 1950 12 15) NOTHING NOTHING NOTHING EMPTY) 4000 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 52.2(2) — the earnings for which a second additional contribution is deemed to have been made for a month of a year with no second additional contribution` EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `s 52.2(3) — a second additional contribution is deemed to have been made for earnings for a month` (YearMonthDay 2025 5 1) (`the deemed-contributions test events` (YearMonthDay 1990 3 10) NOTHING NOTHING NOTHING EMPTY)
#ASSERT NOT `s 52.2(3) — a second additional contribution is deemed to have been made for earnings for a month` (YearMonthDay 2008 2 1) (`the deemed-contributions test events` (YearMonthDay 1990 3 10) NOTHING NOTHING NOTHING EMPTY)
-- a second additional contribution was made: 6000 / 12 = 500
#ASSERT `s 52.2 — the earnings for which a second additional contribution is deemed to have been made for a month` (YearMonthDay 2025 5 1) (`the deemed-contributions test events` (YearMonthDay 1990 3 10) NOTHING NOTHING NOTHING EMPTY) TRUE 6000 EQUALS 500
-- none was made: zero
#ASSERT `s 52.2 — the earnings for which a second additional contribution is deemed to have been made for a month` (YearMonthDay 2025 5 1) (`the deemed-contributions test events` (YearMonthDay 1990 3 10) NOTHING NOTHING NOTHING EMPTY) FALSE 6000 EQUALS 0
-- a month the subsection does not reach: zero
#ASSERT `s 52.2 — the earnings for which a second additional contribution is deemed to have been made for a month` (YearMonthDay 2008 2 1) (`the deemed-contributions test events` (YearMonthDay 1990 3 10) NOTHING NOTHING NOTHING EMPTY) TRUE 9000 EQUALS 0
